# Links that no link checker can verify from any network. Each entry names the
# reason and the date it was confirmed. A link that fails only from GitHub
# runners does not belong here: CI already accepts blocked and slow hosts
# (.github/lychee-ci.toml). Keep entries to exact URLs so other pages on the
# same host are still checked.

# 2026-09-25: GitHub renders pull-request review-comment anchors client-side,
# so fragment checks cannot resolve them. The pull request itself is checked.
https://github\.com/.*/pull/[0-9]+\#discussion_r[0-9]+

# 2026-09-25: McKinsey closes non-browser requests with an HTTP/2 protocol error
# from GitHub runners and from a contributor network alike.
https://www\.mckinsey\.com/careers/interviewing
https://www\.mckinsey\.com/alumni/news-and-events/global-news/alumni-news/barbara-minto-mece-i-invented-it-so-i-get-to-say-how-to-pronounce-it

# 2026-09-25: bot protection answers 403 to scripted requests from GitHub
# runners and from a contributor network, even with a browser user agent.
https://www\.solcom\.de/projektportal/registrieren
https://www\.congress\.gov/

# Own-site and own-repository blob/main URLs are checked against the checkout
# by scripts/check-links.py, including new routes before their first merge.
